cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this model in published work, please cite it, bandsolver, and
  Newman's description of the BAND method (Electrochemical Systems, Appendix C).
title: "nmc111-model: an NMC111 porous-electrode half-cell model with uniform-particle and agglomerate particle scales, solved with Newman's BAND method"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: John
    family-names: Bernard
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-01
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/jcbernard87/nmc111-model"
url: "https://github.com/jcbernard87/nmc111-model"
abstract: >-
  A one-dimensional model of an NMC111 half cell (lithium foil, separator,
  porous cathode) with two particle models: uniform-concentration particles,
  or porous agglomerates of crystals coupled to the electrode through their
  surfaces (a double-porosity model solved with a fully coupled, condensed
  Newton step). Dilute-solution electrolyte transport, electronic conduction
  and Butler-Volmer insertion kinetics are solved by finite volumes, backward
  Euler and Newton's method with the BAND block-tridiagonal solver. It runs
  constant-current, constant-voltage and rest protocols. Fortran, C++ and
  Python implementations read the same input file.
keywords:
  - lithium-ion battery
  - NMC111
  - porous electrode
  - agglomerate model
  - electrochemistry
  - Newman
  - Fortran
  - C++
  - Python
